# Class and Model Initialization

> **Enforced by:** manual review (no reliable automated check)

**Rule:** Use named parameters when initializing ANY class, model, entity, exception, or failure. This applies to all constructors across the project.

### ✅ Good Example
```dart
class UserModel {
  final String id;
  final String email;

  const UserModel({required this.id, required this.email});
}

class ServerException implements Exception {
  final NetworkErrorCode type;
  final int? statusCode;
  const ServerException({required this.type, this.statusCode});
}

final class ServerFailure extends Failure {
  final int? statusCode;
  const ServerFailure({this.statusCode});
}
```

### ❌ Bad Example
```dart
class UserModel {
  final String id;
  final String email;

  const UserModel(this.id, this.email);
}

class ServerException implements Exception {
  final NetworkErrorCode type;
  const ServerException(this.type);
}

final class ServerFailure extends Failure {
  final int? statusCode;
  const ServerFailure([this.statusCode]);
}
```
